A||||3||Gold-86SE||Replacing broken door handle||||5||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||10-23-2001||09:07 PM||||<BR>It is an 85 GT, the driver door handle is broken.<P>Pretend you are standing at the door looking at the handle, the broken portion is on the right side of the handle, under the body of the handle.  Best I can tell, it is a broken hinge pin.<P>Question is how to replace the handle, I have a couple of extra driver doors, from which I can pull a replacement handle. I am just not sure how to do it.<P>BTW, anyone know the cost of a handle from GM?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jake_Dragon||10-23-2001||09:45 PM||||I just removed the screw fasteners on the inside of the door, pull back the door molding (you will probably break one of the clips so be careful) remove the bolt and you should be able to pull the door skin back far enough to remove and replace the handle.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||10-23-2001||09:59 PM||||just don't drop the little clips, they're hard to find down there. Mine was broken the same way. Doni Hagen had one for sale not too long ago.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||10-24-2001||09:21 AM||||<BR>Jake, thanks for the info, I was able to remove the handle last night.<P>maryjane, you are correct, be careful if you drop the clip, I did drop it, but with the brase removed I was able to retrieve the clip.<P>Here is how I did it if anyone is interested:<P>1) remove arm rest<BR>2) remove door handle/release lever shroud<BR>3) release clips holding inner skin to door<BR>4) if you have it, remove cabled mirror<BR>5a) remove inner door skin<BR>5b) if have crank window, just rotate the skin counter clockwise (just do it easy)<BR>6) carefully pull back on the paper between the inner skin and the door<BR>7*) drill out the pop rivets on the cross brase (the brase is about 12" long) - this allowed me to have more space with my hands<BR>8) use an 11mm wrench to remove the nuts holding the handle to the door<BR>9#) release the lock lever from the clip that holds the lever to the handle<BR>10#) gently push the clip out of the handle<BR>11) remove handle from door<P><BR>Install in reverse order<P><BR>7* My door is not yet back together, but I am going to use some shallow fat self-tapping screws to put the brase back on the door<P>9# and 10#  (a flat head screwdriver helps here)<P><p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
